-- title:
--   Kernel of the Tate point classifier lies in every prime power
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity such that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (this is [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22)) with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ be the intermediate field generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise extension along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of $X_{H_1}$ at level $q^2M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $K$ an $A$-algebra in a scalar tower over $L$, and $j \in K$ the element whose Laurent series is the image of the rational $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed nonzero. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, with $K$ and $A$ both $A_0$-algebras in a tower and $A$ module-finite over $A_0$; let $\zeta_A \in A$ have primitive $q$-th root of unity image in $L$ and satisfy $A_0[\zeta_A] = A$; assume $A_0$ contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity and that $\ell$ and $M'$ are units in $A_0$. Assume further the variable-change compatibility hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL` (stability under variable change of: the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point condition, the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$ kernel-polynomial condition, and divisibility of [`ModularCurve.inLineMulPoly`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassH1Pow.html#L18)), a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with invertible discriminant over $A_0$-algebras which is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity section, a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for $\mathcal{G}$ and $q$ which is a section transport, and the hypotheses `hVC`, `hCO` providing graded ring homomorphisms on the graded coordinate rings of projective models realising variable changes and coefficient maps, with the corresponding inclusion of irrelevant ideals. Finally let $P_0$ be an abstract level moduli package over $A_0$ for the level moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓ M' q …` — whose points over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ are variable-change orbits of Weierstrass curves over $T$ with invertible discriminant carrying: for each prime $p \mid M'$ a normalised cyclic-kernel polynomial for $p^{v_p(M')}$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-datum whose two points coincide, lie on the curve and have $x$-coordinate a root of $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$, and a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for $\mathcal{G}$, subject to the link condition that the $\ell$-component polynomial divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓ (ℓ ^ (v_ℓ(M') - 1)) x_P` — with coordinate ring $B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, and let $x$ be a point of this datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the image of the normalised $j$-series under multiplication of all exponents by $q$. Then for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{q}$ of $B_0$ containing the kernel of the classifying $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $B_0 \to K$ attached to $x$, and every natural number $n$, that kernel is contained in $\mathfrak{q}^n$.
--
--   This is the nilpotence statement for the Tate point at the auxiliary $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-type level: the $j$-invariant $j(\mathsf q^{q})$ is transcendental over $A_0$, so the kernel of its classifying map is a minimal prime, and the $\ell$-th roots of unity in $A_0$ produce Lagrange idempotents which force that kernel into all powers of any prime containing it. It feeds the identifications of adic completions of stalks of the moduli ring used in the level-one auxiliary analysis.
